-- title:
--   Local ideles escaping the norm class group in degree two
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a $K$-algebra of degree $[L:K]=2$. Write $H = K^{\times}\cdot N_{L/K}(\mathbb{I}_L)$ for the subgroup of the idele group $(\mathbb{A}_K)^{\times}$ generated by the image of $K^{\times}$ under the diagonal embedding (the subgroup `principalIdeles`) together with the image of $(\mathbb{A}_L)^{\times}$ under the idelic norm attached to `genuineBaseChange K L`, i.e. the unit-group map induced by the algebra norm of $\mathbb{A}_L$ over $\mathbb{A}_K$ for the base-change structure identifying $\mathbb{A}_K \otimes_K L$ with $\mathbb{A}_L$. The assertion is twofold. First, for every finite place $v$ of $K$ (a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$) such that the image of $(L \otimes_K K_v)^{\times}$ under the algebra norm to $K_v^{\times}$ is not all of $K_v^{\times}$, there is $x \in K_v^{\times}$ for which the idele with component $x$ at $v$ and component $1$ at every other finite place and at every infinite place does not lie in $H$. Second, for every infinite place $w$ of $K$ such that the norms of $(L \otimes_K K_w)^{\times}$ do not exhaust $K_w^{\times}$, there is $x \in K_w^{\times}$ for which the idele with component $x$ at $w$ and $1$ elsewhere (the unit `archCentralUnit K w x`) does not lie in $H$.
--
--   This is the non-vanishing of the local-to-global map $K_v^{\times}/N_{v}\to \mathbb{I}_K/K^{\times}N_{L/K}(\mathbb{I}_L)$ at each place of a quadratic extension that does not split, expressing the compatibility of local and global norm residue symbols. It is used to produce idele class characters with prescribed non-trivial local behaviour, via [`NumberField.localChar_ne_one_of_range_norm_ne_top_of_isIdeleClassChar_of_finrank_eq_two`](thm.html#NumberField.localChar_ne_one_of_range_norm_ne_top_of_isIdeleClassChar_of_finrank_eq_two), in the class field theory input to the Langlands–Tunnell step.
-- source:
